      "lastReply": "A VPN is a private tunnel between your device and the internet. Everything you send goes through it, locked so nobody in the middle can read it.\n\nHere is how it goes:\n\nYour device locks (encrypts) your data before it leaves.\nThe locked data travels to the VPN company's computer.\nThat computer unlocks it and sends it on to the website, so the website sees the VPN's address, not yours.\nThe reply comes back the same way.\n\nWhy people use it: safer on public Wi-Fi, and your internet provider can't see which sites you visit. What it doesn't do: it won't stop viruses or hide you from sites you sign in to. You are just trusting the VPN company instead of your provider.\n\n8:33 PM",
